# Accepted container-image findings (docs/security-review.md, ADR 0026).
# Everything else at HIGH or CRITICAL fails CI.

# DS002: the image runs as root. Railway runs one process per container with no
# shell access, and the app needs no privileged work; adding a user would also
# have to move .next and the pnpm store. Revisit before a wider launch.
AVD-DS-0002

# DS026: no HEALTHCHECK in the image. The platform checks /api/health and
# /healthz itself (deploy/railway/*.json), which is the check that matters.
AVD-DS-0026

# esbuild binaries (skipped in ci.yml with --skip-files, as Trivy reports them
# under the Go standard library rather than by CVE we could list here): build
# and migration tooling that bundles only the app's own source.
